    "body": "### Contact Details (e.g. Tox ID or email)\n\ntox:3AE9254DD0EDF34909CAF979BA98557BA6A32A11C43B05144FFDA8792CFFB66300AFB50DA677\n\n### qTox Version\n\nv1.18.3\n\n### Commit Hash\n\nb7802b42dcf5f68474eb4d6db66c004e3ca50848\n\n### Toxcore Version\n\n0.2.20\n\n### Qt Version\n\n6.8.1\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nStart qTox and you will see it if you have a 'private' server and the server is offline.\n\n\n### Observed Behavior\n\nConnects even when my server is offline!\n\n### Expected Behavior\n\nIf I have a server running and configure the app to connect exclusively to my server, it still connects to other servers when my server is offline.\nThis is not the expected behavior.\nFilling in the server settings should prevent connections to other servers.\n\n\n### Reproducibility\n\nAlways\n\n### Operating System\n\nLinux\n\n### Operating System version/distro/name/etc.\n\nWindows 11 Version 23H2\n\n### Relevant log output\n\n```shell\nDHT_Bootstrap runs on Raspberry Pi3b+\nMy IP 86.107.187.54:33445 (it's public so no problem)\n```",
