            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "\r\nMy Raspberry Pi 3B+ functions as a 'server' running the DHT_Bootstrap. People can connect to this DHT_Bootstrap, and in the settings, they can specify that they want to connect only to this 'trusted' DHT_Bootstrap server and no others. \r\nBut that doesn’t work. \r\nIf the Pi is turned off, aTOX still connects to other, potentially less trusted, servers/DHT_Bootstraps. \r\nThis shows that what you set in the settings has no real effect. \r\nDo you happen to have a BTC wallet on your phone? There, you can also specify which (trusted) node you want to sync with and no others. \r\nThe same principle should apply to TOX and aTOX if you can set an IP in the settings.\r\n\r\n\r\n13 sep 2025, 11:15 van ***@***.***:\r\n\r\n> Green-Sky left a comment (TokTok/qTox#606) Can you tell us a little bit more, by what you mean with \"server\" here? —Reply to this email directly, view it on GitHub, or unsubscribe.You are receiving th\r\n> DuckDuckGo>  removed  one tracker. >  > More <https://duckduckgo.com/-hG9NIGbKtVNlV4MWkeULUwy11WPqOuTXuhGw2UUepxzN-TdxMNI2o81TGWhqVzWVFWFQ_BDa_vz0ovrk1A4V6RMRalre72S-tAbSVFgO6NpKDYaVmJqvaDM9NAuRAkbIe9eA06CAFHnj3tDiBBv2xK_R7AGAQS3QnCiwTR3cv-0MQ-ir5uH-sghBU2HmlcmJZHCpKQmnL6YCNn0PV4rSttw4NW6RPQ60pBTB-x_ghUmV9GxCdGl3zoCx0JDQoGMTfL5rhQfT0ugO_0V14Cok-8Y5BrEgG4Bn1gRMEAoaEzMiGB5iIQ6zjPrCPNdQMklDyiMd2jDP5GMvKXNPG-nz8rhgJEzdkKWtTaaiqRP5htTylnLH_Ai-YMOw_oegmbj49XOYRyeh9hUjuzahhYL9C0loTGRrIZwdjIlJIjq2_HR3RcbUdxRIbmmbZCKJ-oNGZQbL29mRVyZcKubhSLMQCA9tlZoHp37-CJMWl-Y7yfS5MUDUtvipxFcYQcWmDDg>\r\n> Report Spam <https://duckduckgo.com/-hG9NIGbKtVNlV4MWkeULUwy11WPqOuTXuhGw2UUepxzN-TdxMNI2o81TGWhqVzWVFWFQ_BDa_vz0ovrk1A4V6RMRalre72S-tAbSVFgO6NpKDYaVmJqvaDM9NAuRAkbIe9eA06CAFHnj3tDiBBv2xK_R7AGAQS3QnCiwTR3cv-0MQ-ir5uH-sghBU2HmlcmJZHCpKQmnL6YCNn0PV4rSttw4NW6RPQ60pBTB-x_ghUmV9GxCdGl3zoCx0JDQoGMTfL5rhQfT0ugO_0V14Cok-8Y5BrEgG4Bn1gRMEAoaEzMiGB5iIQ6zjPrCPNdQMklDyiMd2jDP5GMvKXNPG-nz8rhgJEzdkKWtTaaiqRP5htTylnLH_Ai-YMOw_oegmbj49XOYRyeh9hUjuzahhYL9C0loTGRrIZw