        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "The only way currently to limit who `toxcore` connects too is via a proxy. Or via custom firewall settings or similar.\n\nI do see your concerns with connecting only to trusted nodes etc, but the `DHT` is based around the idea of being fully `P2P`. Also you would not be able to communicate with others, only if the other side also trusts your `tcp-relay` (usually enabled in the `bs node`). The `DHT` is not used to relay messages, only to facilitate connections between peers.\n\nIn the future, clients built with `toxcore` will be able to control which `IP`s you can talk with, but not currently.",
